==========================
echemdb-website Change Log
==========================

.. current developments

v0.2.0
====================

**Added:**

* Added a "Notes and Limitations" and a "Contribute" section to the CV Dataset overview page.
* Added a note to the single component overview page that dissolved gases are only listed if stated in the original publication.
* Added a download section to each entry page, which provides the entry's Data Package (CSV and JSON) as a zip archive, together with a README and a LICENSE.

**Changed:**

* Changed the Contribute page to give an overview of contributions to the echemdb ecosystem, with a section per project linking to its contributing guide.
* Changed the Contribute section of the CV Dataset page to describe the ways to contribute data and link to the contributing guide of the electrochemistry-data repository.
* Changed the title of the CV overview page to "CV Dataset" and updated the description of the tags.
* Changed the curator's comment on entry pages to a warning admonition placed directly below the figure.
* Changed the electrochemistry-data version to 0.10.0.

**Removed:**

* Removed the step-by-step instructions for submitting source data and digitized data from the Contribute page, which are now part of the contributing guide of the electrochemistry-data repository.
* Removed support for Python 3.10, which reached its end of life in October 2026. The website now requires Python 3.11 or later.



v0.1.0
====================

**Added:**

* Added a release workflow with rever.
* Added a pull request template.

**Changed:**

* Changed the deployment to GitHub Pages to only happen when a new version is tagged.

**Fixed:**

* Fixed the Zenodo metadata, which was ignored since it was not named `.zenodo.json`, and its description, which did not describe the content of this repository.


